e physical height, TOP the roof plan, BOTTOM the plausible ground/support footprint. No diagonal corner views, no two facade planes visible together, no invented windows or extra barrels.\n\nRow 3: the source is a horizontal railway platform edge segment with gray stone deck, bright yellow tactile strip and dark metal/wood support. Keep the same material and source pattern. FRONT/REAR show a low horizontal slab edge; RIGHT/LEFT show low horizontal perpendicular edge profiles, not tall posts or broad upright panels. TOP is the deck plan, BOTTOM the physical underside with supports. Keep the tactile surface on TOP and occluded from below, with consistent slab thickness and footprint.\n\nMaintain coherent proportions and repeated details across each row; draw only inferred unseen surfaces conservatively from the supplied source and current views.",
